 another is listed after the shorter one. The source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m.","type":"text"}]}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Traversal\/ST"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedSimplePaths"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:9Traversal19DirectedSimplePathsV","title":"DirectedSimplePaths","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SimplePaths.swift#L222"},"modules":[{"name":"Traversal"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order a depth-first search from the source, taking out-edges in ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges","type"